@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ For a cloud run, use Sites `get_site` for `REDACTED_PROJECT_ID`. Confirm the own
 
 1. Read `/api/market-scanner` first. Run the retrieved Python collector with `--output <scratch-directory> --sessions 60` when fewer than 60 sessions are saved; otherwise use `--sessions 1` to append or replace the latest official session. It downloads official FRED CSV observations, their matching latest observation and next release date from FRED's official series pages, the TWSE holiday calendar/FMTQIK trading dates and same-day MI_MARGN, MI_MARGN_TREND and BFIJ3U raw statistics, the current TWSE/TPEx issuer roster, and date-matched TWSE MI_INDEX / TPEx OTC quotes. The latest date comes from the actual MI_INDEX after-trading report, because STOCK_DAY_ALL can lag after market close. `--macro-only` refreshes the FRED observations and market statistics without recollecting stock history. FRED provider failures are isolated by series; read `macro-collection-status.json` and report remaining failures. FinMind public metadata supplies industry labels only. Retain raw sources and collection status for review. Do not mix TPEx OTC quotes with fixed-price after-hours quotes, or replace a rejected historical date with the latest day. Current classifications do not establish a historical survivorship-corrected universe.
 2. Launch `stty -echo` then `node <retrieved-importer.mjs> <scratch-directory>` in a PTY. At the hidden-stdin prompt supply a single JSON line with the current `token` and the deployed `origin` from `get_site`. Do not include credentials in arguments, files, logs or task text. The importer posts the universe, observations and dated snapshots, then reads saved status. Abort on a rejected write; do not claim a successful update based only on collection. Existing company evidence remains saved; import newly verified filings separately when available.
-3. POST `/api/automation/refresh-all`, poll `/api/automation/status` at 10-second intervals until the matching run has `completedAt`, and read `/api/automation/history`. GET `/api/macro`, `/api/macro-expanded` and `/api/master-model?id=8299` to verify source observation dates, usable coverage, scanner session count and eligible history. An initial cached response may start a background refresh; read again after completion.
+3. POST `/api/automation/refresh-all`, poll `/api/automation/status` at 10-second intervals until the matching run has `completedAt`, and read `/api/automation/history`. Routine patrols add `?compact=1` to the POST and to every status poll (v255): the same checkpoint step runs, but the reply carries only `runId`, `status`, `checkpoint`, `completedAt`, `summary` (the history row plus `gateAuditTotal` and `stockBatch`) and `problems` (coverage rows that are not ok／automatic／not_used). Without the parameter the full payload is returned unchanged. GET `/api/macro`, `/api/macro-expanded` and `/api/master-model?id=8299` to verify source observation dates, usable coverage, scanner session count and eligible history. An initial cached response may start a background refresh; read again after completion.
 4. Preserve the existing macro score rules, raw financial warnings, candidate-only research and Gate criteria. Verify company filings separately before importing additional evidence through `companies`; published actual EPS is not an advance forecast or pre-announcement consensus. Eight distinct verified periods and direct-peer estimates remain required by the relevant Gates. Report unavailable sources and incomplete checks explicitly.
 
 The Worker attempts the same official quote basis during refresh when the imported roster is fresh. The external collector is the fallback for Worker egress failures. Holiday/no-trade observations, suspended securities and newly listed stocks remain excluded or ineligible rather than filled with invented values. No Gemini or model-generated values are involved.
